speechtext:
If the hon. member will permit, I will see if there is any telegram to the Senate committee from the Saint John board of trade. I do not recall having seen any. I do not see here any communication from the Saint John board of trade. I think I
[Mr. Ilsley.}
said that the Halifax board of trade wired that owing to not having had sufficient time to study the bill, the council of the board of trade was not prepared at present to commit itself.
